305 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281176 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c47ab8ca-3bde-5fba-a4a7-31651f3af0b1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281226 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186278790 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281226 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186278940 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281226 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186279658 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281226 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186279814 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281226 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186280726 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281226 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281226 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281226 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186278940 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281226 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e17aea6f-d602-5f51-a2f7-34b15c79c4b3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281559 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186280875 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281559 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162974" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281559 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281559 #edb/ref 1071 "The lamina $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 1\\}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{15{x}^{2}}{y}.$ Find the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281559 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "048f739d-8a1c-5493-b18b-4a60653b31c4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281559 #edb/ref 1074 "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type I plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{15{x}^{2}}{y}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot \\frac{15{x}^{2}}{y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}15{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}15{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}15{x}^{2}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}15{x}^{2}\\cdot [y]_{y={x}^{2}}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}15{x}^{2}\\cdot (1-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}15{x}^{2}-15{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[5{x}^{3}-3{x}^{5}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281586 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186280895 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281586 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163062" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281586 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281586 #edb/ref 1071 "The lamina $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\le y\\le 0\\}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=2{e}^{y}.$ Find the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281586 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "950af147-dd8f-5a17-bc09-5c26666bfffb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281586 #edb/ref 1074 "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type I plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=2{e}^{y}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot 2{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2x{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{0}2x{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}2x[{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{0}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}2x\\cdot [{e}^{y}]_{y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{y=0}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}2x(1-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}2x-2{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{x=1/2}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(1-\\frac{2}{3})-(\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281613 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186280864 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281613 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163152" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281613 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281613 #edb/ref 1071 "The lamina $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,{y}^{2}\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\le y\\le 1\\}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{x}.$ Find the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281613 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "13f35429-2bb3-5bdd-9f21-f76be76ab433" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281613 #edb/ref 1074 "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type II plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{x}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}1\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}[x]_{x={y}^{2}}^{x=1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}1-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{y=1/2}^{y=1} \\\\  & =(1-\\frac{1}{3})-(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{24}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{24}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429353 #edb/ref 1030 0.5 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186429353 #edb/ref 1032 "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account multivariable: 1 rises / 2 eligible passed source activities = 0.500000; nearest selected fraction = 1/2. Crossing activity numbers [2]; waits [2]. Separate account estimates: multivariable=1/2 (1/2). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: True. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.